---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Practical aging-in-place help</p>
    <h1>Make aging at home feel less overwhelming.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Aging at Home Lab creates calm, practical checklists, home-safety guides, and caregiver organization tools for families helping older adults stay safer and more supported at home.</p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button primary" href="/start-here/">Start with the checklist</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/templates/">View templates</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" aria-label="Core guide categories">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Home Safety</h3>
      <p>Room-by-room checklists for bathrooms, bedrooms, kitchens, stairs, entries, lighting, and common fall-risk areas.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Caregiver Organization</h3>
      <p>Binder pages, medication lists, emergency contacts, appointment notes, sibling coordination tools, and weekly care check-ins.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Senior Tech</h3>
      <p>Plain-English decision guides for medical alerts, fall detection, privacy-safe monitoring, medication reminders, and caregiver apps.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Home Modifications</h3>
      <p>Questions to ask before installing grab bars, ramps, stair lifts, shower changes, lighting upgrades, and accessibility improvements.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="callout">
    <h2>Built for the moment when families need a next step.</h2>
    <p>Many families start searching after a fall, hospital stay, missed medication, or hard conversation about independence. Our job is to make the next step clearer without using fear-based selling or pretending a checklist replaces professional judgment.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
